## Interface: 120100
## Title: BestCraft
## Notes: Adds a button to the Place Crafting Order screen that builds and keeps updated an Auctionator shopping list for the right-quality reagents for a crafting order
## Author: Tharavol, Claude
## Version: @project-version@
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\inv_misc_symbolofkings_01
## X-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
## Dependencies: Auctionator
## SavedVariables: BestCraftDB

## X-ReleaseNotes: Adds a button to the customer-side "Place Crafting Order" screen (ProfessionsCustomerOrdersFrame) that builds an Auctionator shopping list for exactly what to go buy -- for every order, recraft or not. Highest-quality reagent per slot, except when the recipe's output has no quality tiers of its own, where the cheapest reagent is picked instead since paying more buys nothing. Optional/finishing reagent slots, reagents already owned (bags/bank/reagent bank/Warband bank), and reagents cheaply available from an NPC vendor are all excluded, with a chat note explaining what was skipped and why. A second order's click merges into the existing list rather than replacing it, and the list updates live as reagents are bought on the Auction House. Guild orders default their commission to 1 silver, and Guild/Personal orders default their Minimum Quality requirement to the recipe's highest tier. Requires Auctionator. Source and issues: https://github.com/Tharavol/BestCraft

